{"title":"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db1bf40a4a8119b9a32be2b01d22c20a12225e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> is a straight angle.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa52cfffceb498b2be1fd235428bb6708a42a530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 54 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 64 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the measures of the angles in the diagram sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db1bf40a4a8119b9a32be2b01d22c20a12225e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> is a straight angle, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff66e1c7b3b5a6ff4a9d9ba675cd5f26c34f0362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 146 = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed463a3aab15f21443e8c4161cca0c5ff1d88dc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 180 - 146 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(E) } 34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"201\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>